<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elisabethenburg Palace</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1682">1682</a>–<a href="/years/1692">1692</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Schloss Elisabethenburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elisabethenburg Palace is the former residence of the dukes of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiningen">Meiningen</a> in Meiningen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>. Duke Bernhard I built it between 1682 and 1692 and named it after his second wife, Elisabeth Eleonore. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> wings remained the seat of the ducal court until 1918 and now house the Meiningen museums, with collections on the court <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and music.</p></div>
